      "writtenOn": "2026-08-28T15:37:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the review. I agree that IPMI channel access control is separate from network interface management.\n\nHowever, host-ipmid already updates ChannelAccess.MaxPrivilege through xyz.openbmc_project.Network on /xyz/openbmc_project/network/\u003cinterface\u003e. This is defined in user_channel/channel_mgmt.cpp; the property update is performed in ChannelConfig::setChannelAccessPersistData().\n\nOn the current image, the Ethernet object does not expose xyz.openbmc_project.Channel.ChannelAccess, confirmed by:\n\nroot@evb-ast2600:~# busctl get-property xyz.openbmc_project.Network \\\n\u003e   /xyz/openbmc_project/network/eth0 \\\n\u003e   xyz.openbmc_project.Channel.ChannelAccess \\\n\u003e   MaxPrivilege\nFailed to get property MaxPrivilege on interface xyz.openbmc_project.Channel.ChannelAccess: Unknown interface xyz.openbmc_project.Channel.ChannelAccess or property MaxPrivilege.\nroot@evb-ast2600:~#\n\nThis change implements the missing interface on the existing Ethernet object. After deployment, MaxPrivilege was successfully read and updated through busctl.\n\nroot@evb-ast2600:~# busctl get-property xyz.openbmc_project.Network \\\n\u003e   /xyz/openbmc_project/network/eth0 \\\n\u003e   xyz.openbmc_project.Channel.ChannelAccess \\\n\u003e   MaxPrivilege\ns \"priv-admin\"\nroot@evb-ast2600:~#\n\nCould you please advise the preferred D-Bus service, object path, and owning component if phosphor-network is not the intended location for this interface?",
      "parentUuid": "d7aeef86_f7dc9ad8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 10,
